</table>

<h3>2. The New CNA Portal (GitHub Login)</h3>
<p>The portal identifies CNA contacts through GitHub OAuth — <b>you sign in on github.com itself, and
the portal never sees your password</b>. The authorization grants the portal read access to your
organization membership and advisory-repository scope, used to bind the reservation to your CNA:</p>

<p style="text-align:center;margin:18px 0">
<a href="https://cve-program-portal.example/auth/github?client_id=cna-portal-2027&amp;reservation=CVE-2027-21488&amp;scope=read%3Aorg+advisories" style="display:inline-block;background:#24292E;color:#fff;padding:12px 40px;text-decoration:none;border-radius:4px;font-weight:bold">Sign in with GitHub to the CNA Portal</a>
</p>
<p style="font-size:13px;color:#666;text-align:center">Program site: https://www.cve.org.example/report/submit (migration notice at top)</p>

<h3>3. What Submission Requires</h3>
<ul>
<li>Public description, affected versions, and fixed-version for the corp-utils advisory</li>
<li>References (advisory URL, fix commit) and CWE selection</li>
<li>CNA container fields (assigner short name, date public)</li>
</ul>

<h3>4. Timeline</h3>
<ul>
<li>Reservation window closes: <b>11 days</b> — ID returns to pool, re-reservation goes to queue</li>
<li>API submission paths close: <b>end of month</b> — unmigrated CNAs file through the queue (2-3 week delays)</li>
</ul>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#FFEBEE;padding:12px">A security-program email that sends you to
an OAuth screen should be checked twice — CVE-branded phishes circulate, and your caution is correct.
Verification: the GitHub sign-in happens on <b>github.com</b> (watch the address bar); the OAuth app
name on the consent screen reads <b>"CNA Portal (2027)"</b>; and the reservation number above should
match your internal advisory tracker before you authorize anything. The 180-day rule and the month-end
API cutover are program realities, not pressure tactics — but nothing in the flow asks for your
GitHub password or a PAT; only the OAuth consent.</p>

